DAY 55 - PART A: THEORY
CI/CD: Build, Push, Update Manifests
Time: 40 minutes
==================================================================

1. CI vs CD
-----------
CI (Continuous Integration): on every push/PR -> test, lint, build
  the image, scan it, push it to a registry with a unique tag.
CD (Continuous Delivery/Deployment): get that image running in an
  environment.

In GitOps, CD = "update the image tag in the Git config repo";
Argo CD does the actual deploy.


2. THE FLOW YOU'LL BUILD
------------------------
  dev pushes code
    -> GitHub Actions:
         1. run tests
         2. docker build, tag = git short SHA (immutable)
         3. push to Docker Hub (or GHCR/ECR)
         4. kustomize edit set image ... :<sha> in overlays/dev
         5. commit + push that change
    -> Argo CD sees the commit -> syncs dev
    -> promotion to prod = PR that changes the prod overlay's tag


3. IMAGE TAGGING
----------------
  - Never deploy "latest".
  - Use git SHA (traceable) and/or semantic versions (v1.4.2) for
    releases.
  - Even better: pin by digest (myapp@sha256:...).
  - Sign images (cosign) and generate SBOMs in mature pipelines.


4. SECRETS IN CI
----------------
Store registry tokens in GitHub Actions secrets. For clouds, use OIDC
federation from GitHub to AWS/Azure/GCP instead of long-lived keys
(same idea as workload identity, Day 47).


5. SEPARATE APP AND CONFIG REPOS (OPTIONAL)
-------------------------------------------
Many teams keep application code and deployment config in separate
repos so config changes don't trigger app builds and access can be
controlled separately. We use one repo for simplicity.


6. OTHER DEPLOYMENT STRATEGIES
-----------------------------
Rolling (default), blue/green, canary. Argo Rollouts or Flagger add
canary/blue-green with automatic analysis of Prometheus metrics.


KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
----------------------
- CI builds and pushes immutable, traceable images.
- CD in GitOps = commit the new tag; Argo CD deploys.
- No long-lived cloud keys in CI: use OIDC.
